    "answer": {
      "short": "$A=2$, $B=3$, $C=-1$.\n\nExpand and equate coefficients, then solve the resulting simultaneous equations.",
      "worked": "Expanding gives\n$$\\begin{align*}2x^2+14x+23&=Ax^2+(6A+B+C)x+(9A+2B+C).\\end{align*}$$\nEquate the coefficients of $x^2$, $x$ and the constant terms:\n$$\\begin{align*}A&=2,\\\\6A+B+C&=14,\\\\9A+2B+C&=23.\\end{align*}$$\nSubstitute $A=2$:\n$$\\begin{align*}B+C&=2,\\\\2B+C&=5.\\end{align*}$$\nSubtract the first equation from the second:\n$$\\begin{align*}(2B+C)-(B+C)&=5-2,\\\\B&=3.\\end{align*}$$\nSubstitute into $B+C=2$:\n$$\\begin{align*}C&=2-3,\\\\C&=-1.\\end{align*}$$\nTherefore, $A=2$, $B=3$ and $C=-1$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
